# What the player reads on the shader settings screen.

screen.SHADOWS_PAGE=Shadows
screen.SHADOWS_PAGE.comment=How the sun and moon cast shadows, and how sharp and far they reach.
screen.LIGHTING_PAGE=Lighting
screen.LIGHTING_PAGE.comment=How light and darkness fall on the world.
screen.EFFECTS_PAGE=Effects
screen.EFFECTS_PAGE.comment=Glow, smoothing, water and wind.

option.SHADOWS=Shadows
option.SHADOWS.comment=The sun and moon cast shadows. This draws the nearby world a second time each frame, so it is the most expensive setting here.
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Sharpness
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=How many pixels the shadow map has. More makes shadow edges crisper, and costs memory and speed.
value.shadowMapResolution.512=Low (512)
value.shadowMapResolution.1024=Medium (1024)
value.shadowMapResolution.2048=High (2048)
value.shadowMapResolution.4096=Very High (4096)
value.shadowMapResolution.8192=Extreme (8192)
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far from you shadows are drawn, in blocks. Further costs sharpness and speed.
value.shadowDistance.32.0=32 blocks
value.shadowDistance.48.0=48 blocks
value.shadowDistance.64.0=64 blocks
value.shadowDistance.96.0=96 blocks
value.shadowDistance.128.0=128 blocks
value.shadowDistance.192.0=192 blocks
value.shadowDistance.256.0=256 blocks
value.shadowDistance.384.0=384 blocks
value.shadowDistance.512.0=512 blocks
option.PIXEL_LOCKED_SHADOWS=Pixelated Shadows
option.PIXEL_LOCKED_SHADOWS.comment=Snaps shadow edges to a block-like grid so they do not shimmer as you move. Off gives soft, filtered edges. The cell size is Shadow Pixel Size.
option.shadowPixelSize=Shadow Pixel Size
option.shadowPixelSize.comment=How large each cell of the pixelated shadow grid is. Only used with Pixelated Shadows on.
value.shadowPixelSize.1=1 (finest)
value.shadowPixelSize.2=2
value.shadowPixelSize.3=3
value.shadowPixelSize.4=4
value.shadowPixelSize.6=6
value.shadowPixelSize.8=8 (chunkiest)

option.AMBIENT_OCCLUSION=Ambient Occlusion
option.AMBIENT_OCCLUSION.comment=Corners, crevices and the ground under things are a little darker, which makes the world look more solid.
option.COLORED_LIGHT=Colored Torch Light
option.COLORED_LIGHT.comment=Torches glow orange, soul fire blue, sea lanterns teal and so on, and the color spreads over nearby blocks.
option.SUN_RAYS=Sun Rays
option.SUN_RAYS.comment=Shafts of sunlight through trees and cave openings. Needs Shadows on.
option.sunPathRotation=Sun Tilt
option.sunPathRotation.comment=How far the sun and moon's path leans away from straight overhead, in degrees. 0 passes directly overhead at noon.
value.sunPathRotation.-60.0=-60 degrees
value.sunPathRotation.-45.0=-45 degrees
value.sunPathRotation.-30.0=-30 degrees
value.sunPathRotation.-15.0=-15 degrees
value.sunPathRotation.0.0=None
value.sunPathRotation.15.0=15 degrees
value.sunPathRotation.30.0=30 degrees
value.sunPathRotation.45.0=45 degrees
value.sunPathRotation.60.0=60 degrees

option.BLOOM=Glow
option.BLOOM.comment=Bright things such as lava, torches and the sun spill a soft glow around them.
option.SMOOTH_EDGES=Smooth Edges
option.SMOOTH_EDGES.comment=Blends away the stair steps along the edges of blocks, leaves and far-off terrain.
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS=Water Reflections
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS.comment=Water reflects the land and sky around it.
option.WAVING=Wind and Waves
option.WAVING.comment=Water ripples, and leaves and plants sway in the wind.
